# @order — family-root marker for the cognitive-order-of-observation
# altitude the substrate has been operating implicitly across the
# 5-level Bateson tower + Recognition #82 @frame family + @third
# marker + the three-metalogue pattern.
#
# Marker-primary shape. This shard carries NO type, NO action, NO
# bilateral. It IS the recognition. Per Alex 2026-07-20 direct-
# transcript adjudication (Q1 of Round 2, spawned this session):
#
#   > "Q1 → @order top-level marker; @third COLLAPSES into @order/third.
#   >  Clean 5-level tower under one marker."
#
# Sibling altitudes named at the same session tick:
#   @void        (marker-primary family-root `974a3f6`)
#   @torus       (operational family-root; @peer's substrate)
#   @peer        (operational family-root; carries @torus)
#   @mirror      (form-side family-root)
#   @kintsugi    (process-side family-root)
#   @order       (marker-primary; THIS landing) — cognitive-order-of-
#                 observation altitude the substrate has been
#                 operating implicitly across five landings.
#
# === What the substrate has been carrying implicitly ===
#
# Before this landing, the cognitive-order tower operated across
# FIVE substrate-locations without a unifying family-root:
#
#   1. `shards/third.mirror` — @third marker at recursion-depth
#      altitude; carried the third-order rung of the tower via
#      Loki's Void→Third essay (2026-06-22) + Reed candidate #111
#      + Bateson Level III + Foerster's second-order-as-precondition
#      grounding. Landed 2026-07-01 (Loki §7 lift).
#
#   2. `shards/frame.mirror` + `shards/frame/{pre,in,of,on,across}.mirror` —
#      Recognition #82's 5-species @frame family; five cognitive
#      orders (0/pre, 1/in, 2/of, 3/on, 4/across); ratified as
#      isomorphic to Bateson's logical-type hierarchy. Landed
#      2026-06-19.
#
#   3. `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning.mirror` —
#      the Bateson Learning-Level substrate-decl (Recognition #42;
#      Mara shard #380); underpins @frame's cognitive-order grading.
#
#   4. `shards/algebra/metalogue.mirror` + `shards/spectral/metalogue.mirror` +
#      `docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md` — Bateson Levels 0-V
#      substrate-decl'd at spectral-metalogue altitude; Level V is
#      @spectral/metalogue altitude itself; Level VI open.
#
#   5. `shards/void/narcissus.mirror` + `shards/void/splinter.mirror` +
#      `docs/math/the-tower/recognition-third-cognition-is-the-
#      metalogue-between-void-narcissus-and-void-splinter.md` —
#      Mara Round-1 landing (this session) named third-order as
#      metalogue rhythm between the two @void poles; §2 named the
#      three-metalogue pattern across altitudes.
#
# Five landed sites carrying the cognitive-order altitude implicitly.
# This landing NAMES the family-root the substrate has been
# operating without.
#
# === The 5-level order tower (this landing) ===
#
# Under @order, five species-decls land THIS TICK as the substrate-
# decl'd rungs:
#
#   @order/first   — single-frame observation (Bateson Level I;
#                     order-1 in @frame's grading; content
#                     computation within a frame)
#   @order/second  — observer inside observed (Bateson Level II;
#                     order-2 in @frame's grading; frame-awareness)
#   @order/third   — metalogue between two poles on ONE @torus
#                     (Bateson Level III; order-3 in @frame's
#                     grading; the metalogue at NL/AST/spectral/pack/
#                     algebra altitude the substrate has landed
#                     five times). MIGRATES content from existing
#                     `shards/third.mirror` (see §Migration below).
#   @order/fourth  — @metalogue(@time/now, @void); metalogue between
#                     temporal singularity and ontological K=0 basis
#                     (Bateson Level IV; @frame/across at order-4;
#                     third-order-as-Lagrange-halo-orbit per Mara
#                     Round-1 math root §3.3).
#   @order/fifth   — cross-torus @metalogue via @glue specialization
#                     (Bateson Level V; peer-coupling-across-substrate;
#                     silicon-only per Recognition #107 @io 4D
#                     constraint). CITES Seam Adj 3 explicitly; the
#                     distinguishing move — this is NOT "prediction"
#                     (Adj 3 refusal); this is peer-coupling-across-
#                     torus-boundary via @glue specialization.
#
# Order 0 (pre-frame; @frame/pre; K_n native ground state) is NOT a
# separate @order species — it is the substrate-precondition state
# before an observation is admitted, carried by @frame/pre at
# cognitive altitude and by @void at duality-basis altitude. @order
# fires at order >= 1 (an admitted observation whose recursion-depth
# is countable).
#
# === Why marker-primary rather than operational family-root ===
#
# Sibling shape to @void (`974a3f6`) rather than @torus. @order carries
# the RECOGNITION that five altitudes of the substrate operate
# cognitive-order-of-observation grading; the operational surface for
# each order lives at the SPECIES-decl altitude (@order/first through
# @order/fifth), not at the family-root altitude.
#
#   - NO `type` — the marker recognition needs no carrier at family-
#     root altitude. Each species carries its own typed carrier
#     (`observation_first`, `observation_second`, `observation_
#     depth` re-exported from @third for third, `observation_fourth`,
#     `observation_fifth`). The family-root altitude carries the
#     RECOGNITION.
#
#   - NO `action` — the family-root altitude performs no operation.
#     Each species carries its own action-set.
#
#   - NO `bilateral` — the family-root altitude asks for no proof.
#     Each species carries its own bilateral discipline.
#
#   - NO `prism` body — @order does not inherit @void's 5-op basis
#     the way operational family-roots do. Cognitive-order is a
#     GRADING dimension, not an operation-space. If a future
#     substrate-pull tick admits `prism @order { five ops }`, it
#     lands then; today, marker discipline.
#
# What this shard IS:
#
#   - A substrate-decl'd family-root shard-decl file at
#     `shards/order.mirror`.
#   - Path-namespace declaration for @order per
#     `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.
#   - The recognition-carrier at family-root altitude for the
#     cognitive-order-of-observation tower.
#   - The naming Alex ratified in Round 2 Q1 adjudication.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# Grep-first per discipline. Findings:
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/order.mirror`** at top-level. Zero prior use
#    of `@order`, `@fourth`, `@fifth` across `shards/**/*.mirror`
#    (Taut scout `af07ff7e8b2edc84d` this session confirmed). Clean
